{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And they beheld</b> — twice in the Masorah: here and the other: ויחזו אלי (Numbers 24:17). (See n.) They are vanity and deception, they said: ויחזו את האלהים — and this was vanity of falsehood. Another interpretation: ויחזו את האלהים ויאכלו וישתו — just as here eating and drinking, so too ויחזו — vanity of falsehood — through eating and drinking, as written: ותחללנה אותי וגו' ובפתותי לחם. That on account of the eating and drinking they gave them, they declared to them false prophecy."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The second occurrence cited as ויחזו לך משאות שוא ומדוחים is obscure; it may refer to a third occurrence or a juxtaposition-reading. The first הכא refers to ויחזו את האלהים in our verse; the other (ואידך) is identified by the explicit quotation ויחזו לי in Numbers 24:17, though the spelling in the text reads לך. Translated hyper-literally; the phrase משאות שוא ומדוחים הם appears to label both occurrences as 'vanity and deception.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:20.057385012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}